// ------------------------------------------------------------
//  Rozdział siedemnasty — Rozmowa w borze. Trzy dni we wsi (siano, Hanka przy
//  łuczywie, Antek, Jagna czeka na dług), a w sercu boru Pan Lasu siada do
//  rozmowy. Jedno pytanie: gdzie jest Marysia (jego dzieci nie mają cienia),
//  kim jest (liczy do tysiąca, potem ktoś inny będzie liczył za niego) albo
//  za co klątwa (trzy sposoby, żeby ją zdjąć). Granica: Dąb, słowo i kapliczki,
//  zielarka, [chata pod lasem] świerk Maćka, tartak. Biały wilk przynosi drugi
//  drewniak: imię (rok wilczego życia), opowieść o Antku albo bezruch (wilk
//  przy Panu Lasu). Zastaw do świtu: siekiera, krzesiwo albo cień.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

=== rozdzial_siedemnasty ===
# tlo: wies_sianokosy
# rozdzial: Chapter Seventeen
# tytul: A Talk in the Forest
For the third day running Zapadlina rose before dawn. The hay lay on the meadows below the village and had to be turned before the dew could rot it, so the men went out with their rakes and the women followed. No one sang. There was only the swish of the rakes and a corncrake in the wet grass. Whenever someone forgot himself and began to hum, his neighbour would nudge him with an elbow and jerk his chin towards Jaromir’s cottage.
Hanka did not go to the meadows. By day she slept for the space of a few prayers at a time, wherever she happened to drop, and at dusk she took a pine splint and walked through the {pani_w_zbozu_noc == z_pochodniami:trampled rye|{pole_zbite_gradem:hail-beaten grain|{pani_w_zbozu_noc == gonil_babe:trodden-down rye|rye}}} to the edge of the young wood. There she sat on a stump, thrust the splint into the earth and, till late into the night, {pani_w_zbozu_noc == za_spiewem:spoke the words of the lullaby into the forest, one after another, in a rasping whisper|hummed a lullaby into the forest, the very one Marysia used to fall asleep to}. Before dawn she came back and set the splint in the window that faced the trees. Then the people going by with their rakes would turn their heads away. Once {trzy_noce == czuwanie_przy_kolysce:Jadwisia|Mrs Wójcik} brought her a pot of porridge; in the morning she took it home again, untouched. # pokaz: luczywo
{ pole_zbite_gradem:
    On Jaromir’s strips lay battered, blackened grain. The neighbours mowed it in a single afternoon, together with the grass from his meadow, so that Hanka would have at least some straw for bedding.
}
Antek came towards evening, sat on the threshold and told her where they had searched that day: by the lake, in the alder thickets, in every barn in Bukowiec. Of the forest he said nothing, and Hanka did not ask.
{ dlug_u_jagny:
    On the third day Jagna drove over from Bukowiec. She did not go into the cottage. She left the cart by the fence, untied a sack of herbs and spent the whole afternoon picking over St John’s wort, stalk by stalk, like someone who has plenty of time and knows exactly why she has come. # pokaz: jagna
}
{ przysiega_ksiedzu:
    The priest in Bukowiec said Mass for the lost child. The people of Zapadlina stood along the church walls and would not meet one another’s eyes.
}
On the third morning, in the heart of the forest, the Lord of the Forest sank to the ground – slowly, with a cracking and groaning of wood, like a barn whose beams have given way – until his face hung over Jaromir as high as a thatched roof.
Jaromir sat down on a root, for his legs would not have held him up much longer anyway. # dalej
